==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmaːðʏr/|lang=is}}
*: {{audio|Is-maður.ogg|Audio (Iceland, Kópavogur)|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|aːðʏr|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|maðr|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*mann-}}, probably ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*mánu-||person}}, {{m|ine-pro|*man-}}.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|m|manns|menn}}

# [[man]], [[human being]]{{jump|is|human being|s}}
#: ''Það tilheyrir náttúru '''mannsins''' að hata þá sem hann hefur sært.''
#:: It belongs to '''human''' nature to hate those that he has hurt.
#* Timothy 2:11-12 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+Timothy+2:11-12&version=NIV English], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1%20Timothy%202:11-12&version=ICELAND Icelandic])
#*: ''Konan á að læra í kyrrþey, í allri undirgefni. Ekki leyfi ég konu að kenna eða taka sér vald yfir '''manninum''', heldur á hún að vera kyrrlát.''
#*:: A woman should learn in quietness and full submission. I do not permit a woman to teach or to have authority over a '''man'''; she must be silent.
# {{context|mainly used with a definite article|lang=is}} [[husband]]{{jump|is|husband|s}}
#: ''Þetta er Geir, '''maðurinn''' minn.''
#:: This is Geir, my '''husband'''.
# {{context|chess|lang=is}} [[chessman]]{{jump|is|chessman|s}}
#: ''Færðu '''manninn''' þinn.''
#:: Move your '''chessman'''.

